More Vulnerabilities That Can Be Paid (501–510)
501. Improper Validation of API Rate-Limit Headers
API Rate Limit Header Manipulation
Attackers manipulate rate-limit headers to bypass request restrictions.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $6,000
502. Insecure Configuration of Reverse Proxies
Reverse Proxy Exposure
Reverse proxy servers expose internal endpoints or sensitive services.
💰 Typical payout: $400 – $7,000
503. Improper Validation of JSON Web Tokens
JWT Signature Bypass
Applications fail to verify JWT signatures correctly, allowing attackers to forge tokens.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $9,000
504. Improper Handling of File Download Authorization
File Download Authorization Bypass
Users download files belonging to other users due to missing authorization checks.
💰 Typical payout: $400 – $7,000
505. Insecure Configuration of Cloud Metadata Services
Cloud Metadata Exposure
Applications allow access to cloud instance metadata that reveals credentials.
💰 Typical payout: $1,000 – $12,000
506. Improper Validation of API Sorting Parameters
API Sorting Parameter Manipulation
Attackers manipulate sorting logic to access restricted records.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $5,000
507. Insecure Configuration of Logging Systems
Logging System Information Leakage
Logs reveal sensitive information such as tokens or internal system paths.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $5,000
508. Improper Security Controls in Email Verification APIs
Email Verification API Bypass
Attackers bypass email verification by manipulating API requests.
💰 Typical payout: $400 – $7,000
509. Improper Handling of Authentication Cookies
Authentication Cookie Misconfiguration
Cookies lack security flags like Secure, HttpOnly, or SameSite.
💰 Typical payout: $200 – $4,000
510. Insecure API Gateway Configuration
API Gateway Security Misconfiguration
API gateways expose internal endpoints or allow unauthorized requests.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $9,000
